---
name: Email auto-credit gates
description: gmail-poll-transactions auto-credit eligibility gates and the body-phone (approx 60% possible user) unique-match fallback
type: feature
---
`_tryAutoCreditOperationalFloat` in `gmail-poll-transactions` auto-credits an incoming MoMo receipt to a user's Operational Float when ALL gates pass: amount>0, transaction_id present, direction='in', channel mtn_momo|airtel_money, receipt <=7 days old, and a user resolves via one of:
1. counterparty phone (last-9 ilike) — confidence high (1.0), phone_source='counterparty'.
2. body-phone fallback — scans counterparty+subject+snippet+raw_body for Ugandan mobiles (regex (?:\+?256|0)?7\d{8}, last9 starts with 7); auto-credits ONLY when every phone found points to exactly ONE known user. This is the UI "possible user approx 60%" signal; recorded confidence medium (0.6), phone_source='body'. Ambiguous (>1 user) logs decision body_phone_ambiguous and skips.
3. MTN name fallback — unique/most-recent-active name match.

Client mirror: autoCreditGateReport in EmailTransactionsPanel.tsx shows a per-row "Why auto-credit was skipped" checklist for every incoming, uncredited, unrouted email.
